# Differences from a character fontconfig will not put in a charset, so no font
# on this side can be matched for it.
#
# fontconfig builds a charset from the cmap but starts it at 0x20, dropping the
# explicit 001D segment Sans Serif Collection carries, so
# CachedFontSet::GetFallbackFontForChar can never reach that family however the
# set is ordered. The Windows side reads the cmap and answers it. U+001D is the
# only character in the BMP where the two disagree.
